    "sentence_translations": [
      "Iron Rooster",
      "",
      "Everyone knows what a rooster (gōngjī) is, but what does “tiěgōngjī” mean?",
      "Tiě is “iron”, gōngjī is “rooster”. So, what could an “iron rooster” be?",
      "Is it a toy? A weapon? Or….? Hahaha! Don’t try to guess.",
      "Actually, “iron Rooster” refers to a type of person.",
      "This type of person is extremely stingy and is unwilling to spend even a cent.",
      "If you want to pluck an “iron rooster’s” feathers, it’s absolutely impossible.",
      "That’s why other than just saying “iron rooster”, ..",
      ".. “iron rooster – not even a feather” is a phrase that is also commonly used.",
      "",
      "For example, “Don’t even think of borrowing money from Little Li. He’s an iron rooster, he won’t give you a cent!”",
      "You can also say, “After talking so much, he still won’t pay. He really is an iron rooster – not even a feather.”",
      "You can also say, “He is an iron rooster who won’t yield even a feather.”",
      "",
      "Do you have any “iron roosters” around you? If you do, quickly tell me stories about them!",
      ""
    ]
  }
